{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789235924,"nonce":"MB1D6UaARZDW6wNCokkOrrQZTok=","message":"Landed in 9a028ea, partially. Fixed: a trailing declaration (var y = x) or control-flow statement no longer leaks a value; an expression body is recognised by the newline rule the reference uses. Kept: a block body still yields its tail expression statement. Full conformance was tried (block bodies return null) and it broke hatch-noise, spatial, template, web and gpu specs; a parser-based scan found 373 sites in packages, site and examples plus 2297 in spec files (1472 of them Test.it blocks ending in Expect.that) that rely on the tail value. Mechanically inserting 'return' at every site preserves behaviour but degrades every published package, so the tail-expression rule stays as a documented extension. Reopen if strict reference semantics are wanted; the scan tool was a 150-line example over the AST and is easy to recreate.","files":null}]}